Subject: [PATCH] stagefright: Opt in to legacy Qualcomm sync-frame thumbnails
Target-repository: frameworks/av
Base-commit: a8732aa05d8920fdbcc56638e5c63036227a5bb9
Path-prefix: a/ and b/ relative to the target repository root

Android 11's library resolution no longer reaches the device's previous
thumbnail configure interposer. Request the existing Qualcomm sync-frame
mode at FrameDecoder configuration time for sync video single-frame reads.

Default: debug.stagefright.qcom_sync_frame=false. Enable explicitly in the
device system.prop; batman_lgu uses true. Require a video/ source MIME,
OMX.qcom.video.decoder.* component, PREVIOUS/NEXT/CLOSEST_SYNC seek, and
both android._num-input-buffers and android._num-output-buffers equal to 1.
Other codecs, non-sync extraction and ordinary playback are unchanged.

Dependencies: independent of 0001. The device must provide the existing
qcom.sync-frame vendor extension (msm8660 media commit f5a78d53ea790aecc13ee13492762ccf98432b24).
The validated batman setup additionally has the separate OMX input-pool
refresh fix in hardware/qcom-caf/msm8660/media, omx_vdec::set_parameter,
when changing resolution. That applied, uncommitted hardware change is
NOT included here; do not treat this directory as its replacement.
Rebuild libstagefright and libshim_thumbnail: the latter includes this
FrameDecoder source. No build hook is added by this patch.
Validation: 1920x1088 MMR and Gallery thumbnails; AVC/MPEG4 Surface decode.

Apply manually from the Android source root:
  git -C frameworks/av apply --check "$PWD/device/lge/batman_lgu/patches/0002-stagefright-opt-in-legacy-QCOM-sync-frame-thumbnails.patch"
  git -C frameworks/av apply "$PWD/device/lge/batman_lgu/patches/0002-stagefright-opt-in-legacy-QCOM-sync-frame-thumbnails.patch"
The commands above expand the patch path before changing directory. A successful
  git -C frameworks/av apply --reverse --check "$PWD/device/lge/batman_lgu/patches/0002-stagefright-opt-in-legacy-QCOM-sync-frame-thumbnails.patch"
means the patch is already present; do not apply it twice.

diff --git a/media/libstagefright/FrameDecoder.cpp b/media/libstagefright/FrameDecoder.cpp
index 734f5bb5aeed932d2540ebfecf546ab6a786adc9..448adb26f04f793fbd125f029a7253db37a361cd 100644
--- a/media/libstagefright/FrameDecoder.cpp
+++ b/media/libstagefright/FrameDecoder.cpp
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include "include/FrameCaptureLayer.h"
 #include <binder/MemoryBase.h>
 #include <binder/MemoryHeapBase.h>
+#include <cutils/properties.h>
 #include <gui/Surface.h>
 #include <inttypes.h>
 #include <mediadrm/ICrypto.h>
@@ -276,6 +277,23 @@ status_t FrameDecoder::init(
         return (decoder.get() == NULL) ? NO_MEMORY : err;
     }
 
+    // Opt in only on devices whose legacy decoder needs its sync-frame mode
+    // to honor the retriever's single-frame buffer requests.
+    const char *mime;
+    int32_t inputBuffers, outputBuffers;
+    if (property_get_bool("debug.stagefright.qcom_sync_frame", false)
+            && mComponentName.startsWith("OMX.qcom.video.decoder.")
+            && mTrackMeta->findCString(kKeyMIMEType, &mime)
+            && !strncasecmp(mime, "video/", 6)
+            && option >= MediaSource::ReadOptions::SEEK_PREVIOUS_SYNC
+            && option <= MediaSource::ReadOptions::SEEK_CLOSEST_SYNC
+            && videoFormat->findInt32("android._num-input-buffers", &inputBuffers)
+            && inputBuffers == 1
+            && videoFormat->findInt32("android._num-output-buffers", &outputBuffers)
+            && outputBuffers == 1) {
+        videoFormat->setInt32("vendor.qcom.sync-frame.value", 1);
+    }
+
     err = decoder->configure(
             videoFormat, mSurface, NULL /* crypto */, 0 /* flags */);
     if (err != OK) {
